================================================================
RADIUMOS SHELL SCRIPT (RSH) REFERENCE
================================================================
File extensions: .rsh  .rash
Comment chars:   %  #
================================================================

VARIABLES
----------------------------------------------------------------
set VAR value               Set a variable
set VAR word1 word2         Set variable to joined words
export VAR value            Alias for set
unset VAR                   Delete a variable
vars                        Print all variables
echo $VAR                   Use variable in output
echo ${VAR}                 Use variable (braced syntax)

BUILT-IN COMMANDS
----------------------------------------------------------------
echo text                   Print text to terminal
echo $VAR                   Print variable value
pause                       Wait for keypress with prompt
sleep milliseconds          Delay (max 10000ms)
delay_ms milliseconds       Alias for sleep
wait_key                    Wait for keypress (no prompt)
clear                       Clear terminal screen
if_exists file command      Run command only if file exists

CONTROL FLOW
----------------------------------------------------------------

  IF / ELSE / ELIF / ENDIF
  -------------------------
  if CONDITION then
      ...
  elif CONDITION then
      ...
  else
      ...
  endif

  Operators:  ==  !=  <  >  <=  >=  &&  ||
  Examples:
    if $X == 10 then
    if $NAME == hello then
    if $A > 5 && $B < 10 then


  WHILE LOOP
  ----------
  while CONDITION
      ...
      break
      continue
  endwhile


  FOR LOOP (range)
  ----------------
  for VAR in START..END
      echo $VAR
  endfor

  FOR LOOP (list)
  ---------------
  for VAR in apple banana cherry
      echo $VAR
  endfor

  LOOP CONTROL
  ------------
  break                     Exit current loop
  continue                  Skip to next iteration


FUNCTIONS
----------------------------------------------------------------
  Define:
    function NAME
        ...
        return
    endfunction

    def NAME
        ...
    enddef

  Call:
    NAME arg1 arg2

  Notes:
    - Functions share global variable scope
    - return exits the function early
    - Recursion is supported up to MAX_CALL_STACK depth


INCLUDES
----------------------------------------------------------------
  ^include "filename"       Include and run another script
  ^include "rsh:main"       Require a main function entry point

  When rsh:main is included the script will only execute
  the function named main and nothing else.


KEYBOARD INPUT
----------------------------------------------------------------
  input VAR                 Read a line from user into VAR
  input VAR prompt text     Print prompt then read into VAR
  input_secure VAR          Read password (masked with *)
  getkey VAR                Wait for one keypress, store char
  getscancode VAR           Wait for key, store raw scancode
  check_key                 Sets KEY_PRESSED to 1 or 0
  read_key_noblock VAR      Non-blocking key read, empty if none
  flush_keyboard            Discard all pending keypresses


WINDOWS
----------------------------------------------------------------
  win_create X Y W H [fg] [bg]
      Create a window, stores ID in $WINID

  win_create_centered W H [fg] [bg]
      Create centered window, stores ID in $WINID

  win_show ID               Draw window to screen
  win_hide ID               Remove window from screen
  win_clear ID              Clear window contents
  win_refresh ID            Redraw window to screen
  win_set_title ID title    Set window title bar text
  win_move ID X Y           Move window to new position
  win_print ID X Y text     Print text at position in window
  win_print_centered ID Y text
                            Print text centered on row Y
  win_draw_box ID X Y W H   Draw a box inside window


MENUS
----------------------------------------------------------------
  menu_create X Y W item1 item2 ...
      Create menu, stores ID in $MENUID

  menu_draw WINID MENUID    Draw menu inside window
  menu_select_next MENUID   Move selection down
  menu_select_prev MENUID   Move selection up
  menu_get_selected MENUID  Store selected index in $SELECTED


BUTTONS
----------------------------------------------------------------
  button_create X Y W H text
      Create button, stores ID in $BUTTONID

  button_draw WINID BUTTONID [selected]
      Draw button (1=selected/highlighted, 0=normal)


PROGRESS BARS
----------------------------------------------------------------
  progress_create X Y W    Create bar, stores ID in $PROGRESSID
  progress_set ID value     Set progress 0-100
  progress_draw WINID ID    Draw bar inside window


NOTIFICATIONS
----------------------------------------------------------------
  notify message [type] [duration]
      type:     info  success  warning  error
      duration: milliseconds (500-10000, default 2000)

  notify_titled title message [type]
      Same as notify but with a title

  toast message             Short pop-up notification


COLORS (for windows)
----------------------------------------------------------------
  black         blue          green         cyan
  red           magenta       brown         light_grey
  dark_grey     light_blue    light_green   light_cyan
  light_red     light_magenta light_brown   white


EXTERNAL COMMANDS
----------------------------------------------------------------
Any RSH command installed in the OS command table can be
called directly by name from a script:

  radifetch
  cowsay Hello
  ls /home/user


AUTOEXEC
----------------------------------------------------------------
On boot the system looks for and runs:
  /bin/autoexec.rsh
  /bin/autoexec.rash   (fallback)


EXAMPLE SCRIPT
----------------------------------------------------------------
% My first RSH script

set NAME World
echo Hello $NAME

for i in 1..5
    echo Count: $i
endfor

input REPLY Enter your name:
echo Nice to meet you $REPLY

if $REPLY == thorne then
    echo Welcome back
else
    echo Hello stranger
endif

================================================================